/*
IEC 60870-5-104 TypeID Summary:

- T1   (M_SP_NA_1)   : Single Point Information – used for ON/OFF status indication (e.g., breaker status).
- T13  (M_ME_NC_1)   : Measured Value, Short Floating Point – used for analog measurements such as power, voltage.
- T30  (M_SP_TB_1)   : Single Point with Timestamp (CP56Time2a) – similar to T1 but includes a timestamp.
- T45  (C_SC_NA_1)   : Single Command – used to control ON/OFF operations of devices.
                        Supports Select/Execute control mode.
- T50  (C_SE_NC_1)   : Set Point Command with Short Floating Point – used for analog control (e.g., power/voltage setting).
                        Supports Select/Execute control mode.
- T100 (C_IC_NA_1)   : General Interrogation Command – requests the device to send all current data points.
- T103 (C_CS_NA_1)   : Clock Synchronization Command – synchronizes the device's internal time with the central system.
- T105 (C_RP_NA_1)   : Reset Process Command – used to clear the device's buffer or reset internal state.
*/
